# Java Clash reference

When changing **game behavior** (movement, pathing, targeting, combat, towers, buildings, spells, elixir, AI, card stats), consult the Java reference first:

**`/home/guru/Downloads/clash-royale-main`**

Do not guess Clash Royale rules from memory — read the matching Java file, then implement or adjust Tiny-Wars logic and tests.

## Key reference files

| Behavior | Java path |
|----------|-----------|
| Troop move, lanes, bridge, targeting | `client/.../runnables/HandleTroopsRunnable.java` |
| Tower attacks | `client/.../runnables/HandleTowersRunnable.java` |
| Building attack + lifetime decay | `client/.../runnables/HandleBuildingRunnable.java`, `core/.../cards/buildings/Building.java` |
| Spells | `client/.../runnables/HandleSpellsRunnable.java` |
| Elixir regen | `client/.../runnables/HandleElixirsCountRunnable.java` |
| Bot AI | `client/.../runnables/HandleNormalBotMoveRunnable.java` |
| Game tick / FPS | `client/.../globals/GlobalData.java` (`FRAME_PER_SECOND = 30`) |
| Troop stats (HP, range, hit speed) | `core/src/main/java/cards/troops/**` |
| Tower stats | `core/src/main/java/towers/` |

## Tiny-Wars mapping

| Java concept | Tiny-Wars |
|--------------|-----------|
| Lanes cols 6, 17 | `LEFT_LANE_COL` (7), `RIGHT_LANE_COL` (16) in `GameConstants.ts` |
| Bridge row y=6 | `RIVER_BRIDGE_ROW` (21) |
| Bridge centre (9,6) → king lock | `isBridgeCenter()` in `LaneMovement.ts` |
| Lane step logic | `getLaneStep()` / `getLaneMarchGoal()` in `LaneMovement.ts` |
| Troop tick | `Troop.ts` |

## Intentional deviations (document in PR/commit if you change these)

- **360° movement**: Java snaps one grid cell per move tick; Tiny-Wars uses continuous `moveTowardDirect` with lane-biased goals. Keep smooth movement — do not regress to 4-direction grid snapping.
- **Chase**: Java troops do not path toward targets; they only fight when already in range. Tiny-Wars chases with `moveFree` when a target is acquired.

When fixing a behavior bug, compare the Java rule first, then add/update a test in `src/**/*.test.ts` (see `no-behavior-regressions.mdc`).
